    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nhues\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\n[randomhue](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/colors/randomhue.lua) with [CoC](https://github.com/neoclide/coc.nvim) link to `DiagnosticXXX` instead of `DiagnosticUnderlineXXX`, causing it to be invisible.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1ad462d0c4a9c83a2202f96504aba149705485d1/lua/mini/hues.lua#L1375-L1379\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev+2384-g848fc8ede\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. `colorscheme randomhue`\r\n3. `highlight CocWarningHighlight`\r\n\r\nNotice that it link to `DiagnosticXXX` instead of `DiagnosticUnderlineXXX` \r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nDiagnosticUnderline with Coc\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/2e64ef13-f72e-425a-a7e2-732d0092d8b2)\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/91024200/7427ed89-e93d-487d-8381-f09a346ce7d2)\r\n",
